 tech university we did courses on  setting up a company like how to design  a product what benefits it will bring  etc it wasn't i open up since 2015 geha  has been supported by IT specialist  folclore van mainly I came here because  of I mean the vision of jahar about like  a new innovative way to tackle malaria  and whilst we know excited to to  children to join jail and and see how we  can work together to to fight malaria  from closure on takes care of the  financial side because research is  expensive I mean in Burkina Faso it's  pretty difficult to find to fight  funding for innovation you find money  for development projects so if you want  to dig you know a wholesaler to get to  find water or if you want to build  school you can find money if you want to  innovate to create something you know  like what we do it's more difficult in  early 2015 the project was at risk  because there were no funds then a  crowdfunding campaign brought in more  than 70 thousand euros I always tell  myself if I can save one life or two or  perhaps even 100,000 my greatest dream  will come true and the sooner it does  the better because every two minutes a  child still dies of malaria
 

